6. **RD-839's free-text backstop has blind shapes — READ-ONLY-INFERRED, `057a69d:backend/server.js` `withholdOutsidePaths`:** `v.replace(/(^|[\s:'"(=])(\/[^\s'"),]+)/g, …)` matches an absolute token ONLY after start-of-string, whitespace, `:`, `'`, `"`, `(` or `=`. **(a)** a path after `[`, `<`, `{`, `,` (no space), a backtick or `@` is not matched; **(b)** the token stops at whitespace, so a path holding a SPACE that is not in the "known" set (the `file` label, `survivingTarget`, or the text after the error's LAST `": "`) is withheld only up to the space and **its tail leaks**; **(c)** only TOP-LEVEL string fields of each entry are rewritten — a path inside a nested object or array value is untouched; **(d)** `...erasure.getStatus()` is spread unfiltered (`reason`, `requestedBy` are operator text). Whether the PRODUCT ever writes (a)-(c) is UNMEASURED — row b3 drives every shape the product writes FIRST, then the planted shapes. Ruling T4.
