### How to build your trees
- **No worktree is created in the NexusAI repo, and you never work in its `2_Project_Files` checkout or any builder `worktrees/` directory.** In that repo use ONLY read verbs: `show`, `diff`, `log`, `ls-tree`, `cat-file`, `grep`, `ls-remote`, `rev-parse`, `merge-base`, `rev-list` (plus `count-objects` for §7.9). **NEVER `fetch`, `pull`, `push`, `checkout`, `worktree`, `commit`, `stash`, `gc`, `merge`; and `merge-tree --write-tree` ONLY with `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY=<your own scratch dir> GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES=<repo>/.git/objects`, or in your own `--shared` clone.**
- **Every tree is K1** — `git clone --shared --no-checkout <repo> <dir>` then `checkout` in YOUR clone (origin removed; local identity; `gc.auto 0`; `core.fsmonitor false`; hooks off), under a fresh `mktemp -d` in `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/!CODING/Testing Agent MAIN/projects/nexusai/qa-trees/batch22.XXXXXX/`. Status-check before use.
- **Each tree is EXCLUSIVE to this gate and to ONE purpose.** A fresh arm per mutant; never reuse a mutant tree for a clean arm; `batch22`-prefixed directories only; never run in, write to, or clone node_modules FROM another gate's trees.
- **The red-at-parent trees (each committed IN YOUR CLONE ONLY, hashed after the change):** **A (i):** head tree with ONLY `backend/dataErasure.js` → `343348d` (`b214f6f`'s product; rd838 H × 4, C1-256, C2-256 red); **A (RD-640's own red):** head tree with ONLY `dataErasure.js` → `1f708e2` (M0's; gate 19 a0 measured 13 rd640 cells red there); **A (ii):** `b214f6f`'s OWN tree on `e9063d4` (T2); **B:** head tree with ONLY `backend/server.js` → `c8ca2b3`; **C:** head tree with the FIVE product/style files at `08a81e2`'s blobs (`e2aaa46`, `451c7c6`, `de6e0fe`, `d94423a`, `f614781`).
- **RD-721's vendored bytes (T6 (a)):** `git cat-file -p 7d93a97888561db08eb7a166abad952824374186` and `52b12533e4da87cb83e50039430cd027b48f931a` into YOUR scratch dir, sha256 checked against WRONG 10's values BEFORE use; served only to YOUR page by `route.fulfill`.
