## 2. Why these tiers, and who is waiting — severity rules
- **RD-838 TIER 1:** any target outside DATA_DIR touched, followed, read or written (a3) is a **Blocker**; a link whose chain still reaches data unlinked and/or recorded `purged` (F-640-1's class, any level, any shape) is a **Blocker**; a re-drive that turns a kept failure into `purged` while data is reachable is a **Blocker**; a chain to NOTHING kept forever (F-640-2's class) is a **Major**; gate 19's reproducers NOT red at `b214f6f` (the control) makes a2 VOID, never a pass; a declared mutant not red as claimed is a **Minor**; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 failing on MT-BA/MTF is a **Major**; a READY claim that is false is a **Minor**. **A NO GO returns to Tuesday — no round 4 (C-213).**
- **RD-839 TIER 1:** an outside absolute path in the anonymous window body for a product-written shape is a **Major** (T4; for a planted-only shape, named/Minor); a signed-in admin, or an open-mode caller after setup with users, losing ANY path is a **Major**; the stored record changing by one byte is a **Blocker** (C-139 ADDENDUM 3; RD-684's re-drive reads it); `pathsWithheld` missing when something was withheld, or present when nothing was, is a **Minor**; a 500 where the base answered 200 is a **Major**; a C-212 conflict in any file other than the counts file is a **STOP**; a declared mutant not red as claimed is a **Minor**; a C-68 cell failing on MT-B/MT-BA/MTF is a **Major**.
- **RD-840 + RD-841 TIER 2:** any declared colour in a changed rule that does not resolve to the style guide is a **Major** (Tuesday's brief: *"any colour that does not resolve to the guide is a Major"*); the dark tile off `#262626` is a **Major** (Q1); a control losing its aria-label, `nx-eye` hook, `data-kpi-code` or its evidence card, or the row's accessible text gaining a character, is a **Major**; the icon not exactly `<i class="bi bi-info-circle" aria-hidden="true">` is a **Major** (Q2); values not aligned or a tile row not filling its pane (measured in the browser) is a **Major**; the DOM order changed is a **Major** (RD-279); a contrast below 4.5:1 for body text on the new ground is a **Major**; the counts in the generator and BRAND.md not moving together is a **Minor**; a C-68 cell failing on MTF is a **Major**; a READY claim that is false is a **Minor**.
- **Who is waiting:** RD-838's and RD-839's merge author is **NexusAI-N (S94N)**; RD-840 + RD-841's is **NexusAI-O (S96O)**, whose screenshots go to Kam through Tuesday before any demo deploy.

## 2a. LEGITIMATE SHAPES — required measurements, row by row
